    "title": "U-M Health Sparrow breaks ground on $83M Lansing psychiatric facility - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Shajaka Shelton ,\n1 hours ago LANSING, Mich. (WLNS) — The Lansing area is now one step closer to expanded mental health care access, with the University of Michigan Health-Sparrow breaking ground on a new $83 million psychiatric facility Wednesday.\nThe new location, named the Janice M. Granger Behavioral Health Building , will be located near the intersection of Pennsylvania Avenue and Jerome Street, behind the hospital.\nUM Health-Sparrow plans new mental health, surgery center. (Image: U-M Sparrow Health) Featuring 64 beds, Sparrow says the facility, expected to open in 2028, will expand access to psychiatric care for patients of all ages, with a “park-like setting with indoor and outdoor gardens and light-filled spaces intended to create a healing environment.”\n“It’s taken us awhile to get to this point, but it was well worth the time and effort,” said Margaret Dimond, Regional President of U-M Health. “We’re here today to break ground and take the first steps toward construction of the Janice M. Granger Behavioral Health Building, which will bring much-needed new services to our most vulnerable patients.”\nUM Health-Sparrow plans new mental health, surgery center Sparrow says the facility is named for Janice M. Granger, who, with Alton L., is responsible for the largest donation in the organization’s history.\nSparrow also broke ground on a new $60 million surgery center in the city last month, which will boast operating rooms, a new MRI and other features, expected to ease capacity issues and reduce wait times at the city’s hospital.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WLNS 6 News.",
    "summary": "1 hours ago LANSING, Mich. (WLNS) — The Lansing area is now one step closer to expanded mental health care access, with the University of Michigan Health-Sparrow breaking ground on a new $83 million psychiatric facility Wednesday. UM Health-Sparrow plans new mental health, surgery center.",
